<body>

<h1>Vapor</h1>
<div class="version">Version __VERSION__ (__BUILD__)</div>
<p>Voice-to-text dictation &amp; AI prompt compression for macOS.</p>

<h2>Installing the App</h2>
<div class="step">
  <strong>1. Drag Vapor.app to your Applications folder.</strong>
  <p>On first launch, macOS may prompt you to confirm you downloaded the app from a trusted source. Click Open.</p>
</div>

<h2>Quick Start</h2>
<p>Vapor works immediately with Apple's on-device AI. No downloads or API keys required.</p>
<div class="step">
  <strong>1. Grant permissions</strong>
  <p>On first launch, Vapor asks for <strong>Microphone</strong> and <strong>Speech Recognition</strong> access. Both are processed entirely on-device.</p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>2. Dictate a prompt</strong>
  <p>Hold the <kbd>Fn</kbd> key and speak. Release to commit the text to the editor.</p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>3. Compress &amp; copy</strong>
  <p>Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Return</kbd> to compress the prompt and copy it to the clipboard. Paste into any AI chat interface.</p>
</div>

<h2>Compression Backends</h2>
<p>Choose a compression backend in <strong>Settings &gt; Compression</strong>:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Backend</th><th>Setup</th><th>Cost</th></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Foundation Models</strong> <span class="tag">DEFAULT</span></td><td>None — built into macOS 26+</td><td>Free</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Local LLM (Qwen 2.5-7B)</strong></td><td>One-click download (4.7 GB) in Settings</td><td>Free</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Ollama</strong></td><td>Pull models from Settings &gt; Ollama Models</td><td>Free</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>OpenRouter</strong></td><td>Paste API key from openrouter.ai</td><td>~$0.01/1M tokens</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Rule-Based</strong></td><td>None — always available as fallback</td><td>Free</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Best quality on-device: Local LLM</h3>
<p>In Settings &gt; Compression, select "Local LLM (On-Device)" and click "Download Qwen 2.5-7B (4.7 GB)". Requires ~5 GB disk and a Metal GPU (any Apple Silicon Mac).</p>

<h3>Best quality overall: OpenRouter</h3>
<p>Get an API key from <a href="https://openrouter.ai">openrouter.ai</a>. Paste it in Settings &gt; Cloud. Then select "OpenRouter" in Settings &gt; Compression and pick a model.</p>

<h3>Using Ollama models</h3>
<p>Vapor bundles Ollama and manages it automatically. Go to Settings &gt; Ollama Models and click "Pull" on a recommended model. Recommended: <code>gemma4:e4b</code> (3.2 GB, best balance of speed and quality).</p>

<h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Shortcut</th><th>Action</th></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Fn</kbd> (hold)</td><td>Dictate</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Return</kbd></td><td>Compress &amp; copy</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd></td><td>Copy original</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd></td><td>Copy &amp; clear</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Opt</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Focus Vapor from any app</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>\</kbd></td><td>Toggle compact / full</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd></td><td>Focus screenshot shelf</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Option</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd></td><td>Focus context tray</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>E</kbd></td><td>Context explorer</td></tr>
  <tr><td><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Y</kbd></td><td>Prompt history</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Browser Extension (Optional)</h2>
<p>Inject compressed prompts directly into AI chat interfaces in Chrome.</p>
<div class="note">
  <strong>Important:</strong> Before loading the extension, copy the <code>Browser Extension</code> folder from this DMG to a permanent location on your Mac (e.g. your Documents folder). Chrome cannot load extensions directly from a disk image — the folder must reside on a local drive.
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>1. Copy the extension to your Mac</strong>
  <p>Drag the <code>Browser Extension</code> folder from this DMG to <code>~/Documents/Vapor Browser Extension/</code> (or anywhere on your local drive).</p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>2. Open Chrome and go to <code>chrome://extensions/</code></strong>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>3. Enable Developer mode</strong>
  <p>Toggle "Developer mode" in the top-right corner.</p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <strong>4. Load the extension</strong>
  <p>Click "Load unpacked" and select the <code>Vapor Browser Extension</code> folder you copied in step 1.</p>
</div>
<div class="note">
  The browser extension requires Vapor to be running. It communicates with the app on <code>localhost:8766</code>. Enable browser integration in Vapor's Settings &gt; Browser.
</div>

<h2>More Help</h2>
<ul>
